# Stub inventory for the `common` role's offline dry-run smoke test
# (spec lxc-docker-base-template, task 4.2, requirement 7.2; design Testing
# Strategy Tier 1).
#
# This inventory exists ONLY to give `ansible-playbook --syntax-check` and
# `--check` a target to bind the role against — it performs NO host mutation.
# It points at the loopback host with a local connection so no SSH, no remote
# host, and no real infrastructure is ever touched. The conventional Ansible
# role `tests/` layout (tests/inventory + tests/test.yml) is used.
#
# `--check` against this local host WILL evaluate tasks; some (apt installs,
# docker daemon/Compose probe) may report errors on the authoring host because
# it has no Docker apt repo, may lack apt privileges, and runs no docker daemon.
# Per requirement 7.2 the goal is to confirm task WIRING / syntax / module
# resolution, not to converge this host — so `--syntax-check` is the hard gate
# and `--check` is best-effort wiring confirmation. The role's own bake/LXC
# guards (`failed_when: false` on the systemd + Compose-probe tasks) keep such
# environmental errors from being role defects.
localhost ansible_connection=local
